# There was no .gitignore in this repo, and `git ls-files` showed why that matters:
# `.env`, `.env.bak.*` and all 5,500 files of `.venv/` were tracked. The repo has no
# remote and two commits, so nothing has left this machine -- but the next `git add`
# would have committed provider keys again. This stops that. It does not remove what
# is already in history: untracking (`git rm --cached`) and rewriting the two commits
# are separate decisions, and the second one is destructive, so neither is done here.

# Credentials. Never tracked, in any form.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
tools/.autobuild-env

# Python environment and bytecode. Regenerable; 5,500 files of it.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

# Node and build output.
node_modules/
dist/
apps/desktop/tests/.build/

# The build supervisor's own logs and lock.
.autobuild/
tools/.autobuild-stop

# Local databases, captures and scratch.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
